{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Hani ibn Urwah (a.s.)",
  "data": "After the ziyarat of Muslim ibn Aqil (a.s.), stand at the tomb of Hani ibn Urwah, greet the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), then say:\nسَلَامُ اللّٰهِ الْعَظِيْمِ وَصَلَوَاتُهٗ\nSALAAMULLAAHIL A'ZEEMI WA SALAWAATUH\nPeace of Allah the All-great and His blessings\nعَلَيْكَ يَا هَانِيَ بْنَ عُرْوَةَ\nA'LAYKA YAA HAANIYABNA U'RWAH\nbe upon you, O Hani son of Urwah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْعَبْدُ الصَّالِحُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL A'BDUS SAALIH\nPeace be upon you, O righteous servant (of Allah),\nالنَّاصِحُ لِلّٰهِ وَلِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَلِاَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAN-NAASIHU LILLAAHI WA LIRASOOLIHEE WA LI-AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\nwho acted sincerely for the sake of Allah, His Messenger, the Commander of the Faithful,\nوَالْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ\nWAL HASANI WAL HUSAYNI A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nal-Hasan, and al-Husayn, peace be upon them.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قُتِلْتَ مَظْلُوْمًا\nASH-HADU ANNAKA QUTILTA MAZLOOMAA\nI bear witness that you were slain wrongly.\nفَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ وَاسْتَحَلَّ دَمَكَ\nFALA'ANALLAAHU MAN QATALAKA WASTAHALLA DAMAK\nSo, may Allah curse those who slew you and dared to shed your blood\nوَحَشٰى قُبُوْرَهُمْ نَارًا\nWA HASHAA QUBOORAHUM NAARAA\nand may He stuff their graves with fire.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ لَقِيْتَ اللّٰهَ وَهُوَ رَاضٍ عَنْكَ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA LAQEETALLAAHA WA HUWA RAADIN A'NK\nI bear witness that you met Allah while He is pleased with you\nبِمَا فَعَلْتَ وَنَصَحْتَ\nBIMAA FA'ALTA WA NASAHT\nfor what you did and for your sincere counsel.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ بَلَغْتَ دَرَجَةَ الشُّهَدَاۤءِ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKA QAD BALAGHTA DARAJATASH SHUHADAA'\nAnd I bear witness that you have attained the rank of the martyrs,\nوَجُعِلَ رُوْحُكَ مَعَ اَرْوَاحِ السُّعَدَاۤءِ\nWA JU'ILA ROOHUKA MA'A ARWAAHIS SU'ADAA'\nand your soul has been placed with the souls of the blessed\nبِمَا نَصَحْتَ لِلّٰهِ وَلِرَسُوْلِهٖ مُجْتَهِدًا\nBIMAA NASAHTA LILLAAHI WA LIRASOOLIHEE MUJTAHIDAA\nfor you painstakingly acted with sincerity for Allah and for His Messenger,\nوَبَذَلْتَ نَفْسَكَ فِي ذَاتِ اللّٰهِ وَمَرْضَاتِهٖ\nWA BADHALTA NAFSAKA FEE DHAATILLAAHI WA MARDAATIH\nand sacrificed yourself for the sake of Allah and for the sake of attaining His pleasure.\nفَرَحِمَكَ اللّٰهُ وَرَضِيَ عَنْكَ\nFARAHIMAKALLAAHU WA RADIYA A'NK\nSo, may Allah have mercy upon you and be pleased with you,\nوَحَشَرَكَ مَعَ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nWA HASHARAKA MA'A MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIT TAAHIREEN\nmay He include you with the group of Muhammad and his Immaculate Household,\nوَجَمَعَنَا وَاِيَّاكُمْ مَعَهُمْ فِيْ دَارِ النَّعِيْمِ\nWA JAMA'ANAA WA IYYAAKUM MA'AHUM FEE DAARIN NA'EEM\nand may He gather us with you and them in the Abode of Bliss.\nوَسَلَامٌ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ\nWA SALAAMUN A'LAYKA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon you.\nThen pray two units and give them to Hani ibn Urwah as a gift, and ask Allah for whatever you need.\nWhen you leave, bid him farewell as you did Muslim ibn Aqil, with the farewell of al-Abbas (a.s.), at the end of [Ziyarat of Hazrat Abbas (a.s.) — Karbala](AG18).",
  "merits": "Mafatih al-Jinan gives this ziyarat at the tomb of Hani ibn Urwah, after the ziyarat of [Muslim ibn Aqil (a.s.)](G60) by Masjid al-Kufah."
}
